Z||000000||Zman302||06-03-2000||12:07 AM||||This is kinda a stupid question, i am wondering if you can change the grease/fluid in the steering rack.  I've got about 125000 on my 84 and would like to keep things working for that many more.  Any info would be greatly appreciated.||||reg||5
Z||000001||terryk||06-04-2000||02:05 AM||||I'm in the middle of rebuilding two 86 SE racks. You can change the grease, but it would require the rack to be completely dissassembed. If the boots and pinion gear seal is (are/am) good, the grease doesn't take any beating and is likley fine.<P>Unless it is giving you problems, leave it. You should check the inner tie rods with that many miles on it.<P>One interesting note. Both racks had water in them. Strange. Boots and seal was/were/are/am good.<BR>||||reg||1
